{"url": "https://markaicode.com/benchmarks/qdrant-vs-pgvector-performance/", "crawled_content": "# Qdrant vs pgvector Benchmark 2026: Throughput & Latency

Hook: the two most-cited public benchmarks on this pairing disagree sharply on which engine "wins," and the disagreement itself is the most useful data point. Qdrant tends to win on tail latency; pgvector — especially paired with the pgvectorscale extension — has posted an order-of-magnitude throughput lead in at least one independently published test. Neither result generalizes to every workload, and this article says so at every number.

**Sourcing disclaimer:** This is not a first-party lab benchmark. We do not have access to run a controlled Qdrant vs. pgvector test on dedicated hardware for this article, so every figure below is attributed to a specific public source — Qdrant's own published benchmarks, Tiger Data's (Timescale's) comparison, or independent community testing. Where sources disagree, we show the disagreement instead of picking a winner. If you need numbers for a purchasing or architecture decision, treat all"}
